55,48,163,.35)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5)\';\">CUET PG Response Sheet</a>\r\n    <a href=\"https://www.collegenirnay.com/news/rajasthan-bstc-2026-notification\" style=\"color:#fff;text-decoration:none;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5);border-radius:12px;min-height:64px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:12px;font-size:clamp(13px,2.8vw,14px);font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;transition:all .35s cubic-bezier(.17,.67,.83,.67);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35);\" onmouseover=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(-6px) scale(1.02)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 20px 40px rgba(55,48,163,.35)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#4338ca,#6366f1)\';\" onmouseout=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(0) scale(1)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5)\';\">Rajasthan BSTC 2026 Notification</a>\r\n    <a href=\"https://www.collegenirnay.com/news/ugc-releases-new-guidelines-universities-2026\" style=\"color:#fff;text-decoration:none;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5);border-radius:12px;min-height:64px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:12px;font-size:clamp(13px,2.8vw,14px);font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;transition:all .35s cubic-bezier(.17,.67,.83,.67);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35);\" onmouseover=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(-6px) scale(1.02)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 20px 40px rgba(55,48,163,.35)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#4338ca,#6366f1)\';\" onmouseout=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(0) scale(1)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5)\';\">UGC Releases New Guidelines</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>','/uploads/blogs/1783144634682-626302137.webp',NULL,'Why Choose Poornima University Jaipur? Courses, Placements & More','Explore why Poornima University Jaipur is a top choice for higher education. Learn about courses, campus life, scholarships, placements, and career opportunities.',1,1,'2026-07-04 05:57:14','Blog','Poornima University, Jaipur, Higher Education, Courses, Campus Life, Scholarships , Placement Support','Yash Bharadwaj','5',1,'published','2026-07-04 00:00:00'),(40,'Apex University Jaipur Admission 2026: Complete Guide to Courses, Eligibility, Fees, Scholarships and Application Process','apex-university-jaipur-admission-courses-eligibility-fees-scholarships','Planning to take admission to Apex University Jaipur in 2026? This comprehensive guide covers everything you need to know, including UG, PG, diploma, and Ph.D. courses, eligibility criteria, fee structure, scholarships, admission process, important dates, required documents, campus facilities, placements, and career opportunities. Whether you\'re applying through CUET, AUCET, or direct admission, this guide will help you understand the complete admission procedure and choose the right program for your academic and career goals','<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"en\">\r\n<head>\r\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\" /><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"/>\r\n<title>Apex University Jaipur Admission 2026: Complete Guide to Courses, Eligibility, Fees, Scholarships and Application Process</title>\r\n<style>html{scroll-behavior:smooth;}summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none;}</style>\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin:0;\">\r\n    This <strong>Apex University Admission Guide</strong> covers the complete picture for <strong>Apex University Jaipur Admission 2026</strong> — what you actually need to know before applying. Apex University, established in 2018 at V.T. Road, Sector-5, Mansarovar, Jaipur, has grown quickly into one of Rajasthan\'s most recognised new private universities: UGC-recognised, approved by AICTE, BCI, PCI, NCTE, RCI, INC, and RNC, ranked #1 among emerging universities in Rajasthan by Forbes India, and operating a 30-acre campus with 43+ programmes and 500+ placement recruiters. This guide covers <strong>Apex University Jaipur Courses</strong> at both UG and PG levels, <strong>Apex University Eligibility</strong> criteria, the complete <strong>Apex University Fees</strong> structure, <strong>Apex University Scholarships 2026</strong> across eight schemes, and the step-by-step <strong>Apex University Application Process</strong> \r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">What We Cover</h2>\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;margin:0;\">\r\n    <li><a href=\"#about\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">About Apex University — Why It\'s Distinct in Jaipur</a></li>\r\n    <li><a href=\"#ug-courses\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">Apex University UG Courses — Eligibility and Entry Routes</a></li>\r\n    <li><a href=\"#pg-courses\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">Apex University PG Courses — Eligibility and Entry Routes</a></li>\r\n    <li><a href=\"#fees\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">Apex University Fees — Programme-Wise Breakdown</a></li>\r\n    <li><a href=\"#scholarships\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">Apex University Scholarships 2026 — All Eight Schemes</a></li>\r\n    <li><a href=\"#application\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">Apex University Application Process — Step by Step</a></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"about\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">About Apex University — Why It\'s Distinct in Jaipur</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <strong>Apex University Jaipur Admission 2026</strong> is one of the few new-generation private university admissions in Rajasthan that genuinely offers a wide programme spread at competitive fees. Before breaking down the details, here is the honest institutional picture:\r\n  </p>\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li><strong>Recognition and approvals:</strong> UGC-recognised university under the Rajasthan State Legislature Act No. 27 of 2018; AICTE (Engineering), BCI (Law), PCI (Pharmacy), NCTE (Education), RCI (Rehabilitation), INC (Nursing), RNC (Nursing) approved across respective disciplines</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Rankings:</strong> #1 among emerging universities in Rajasthan by Forbes India; member of Association of Commonwealth Universities (ACU) and Association of Indian Universities (AIU)</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Campus:</strong> 30-acre campus at Mansarovar, Jaipur — central city location, not a distant highway campus, which matters for day-scholars and city residents</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Scale:</strong> 43+ programmes across 16 streams; 4,000+ students placed historically; 5,000+ internship offers facilitated</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Placements:</strong> Highest package ₹36 LPA; average ₹10 LPA; 500+ recruiters including Cisco, Infosys, Tech Mahindra, Wipro, ICICI Bank, TCS, Cognizant, Accenture, and more</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Admission model:</strong> 50% seats filled through AUCET (Apex University Common Entrance Test); 50% through CUET UG/PG — giving candidates without CUET scores full access to half the seat pool</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:0;\">\r\n    The honest note for <strong>Apex University Admission 2026</strong> candidates: Apex is a young institution (founded 2018) — the placement network, alumni depth, and research infrastructure are still maturing relative to 20+ year-old private universities. The value proposition is competitive fees, city-centre location, and a broad programme range for a growing institution.\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div id=\"ug-courses\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">Apex University UG Courses — Eligibility and Entry Routes</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <strong>Apex University UG Courses</strong> span a genuinely wide range for a single 30-acre Jaipur campus:\r\n  </p>\r\n  <div style=\"overflow-x:auto;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;min-width:620px;font-size:14px;\">\r\n      <tbody>\r\n        <tr style=\"background:#3730a3;color:#fff;\"><th style=\"padding:10px;text-align:left;\">Course</th><th style=\"padding:10px;text-align:left;\">Duration</th><th style=\"padding:10px;text-align:left;\">Eligibility</th><th style=\"padding:10px;text-align:left;\">Entry Route</th></tr>\r\n        <tr style=\"background:#f9f9f9;\"><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">BTech (CSE, ECE, ME, CE, IT and more)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">4 years</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">10+2 PCM 50% (45% reserved)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">CUET / AUCET / JEE Main</td></tr>\r\n        <tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">BCA</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">3 years</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">10+2 any stream with Maths 50% (45%)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">CUET / AUCET</td></tr>\r\n        <tr style=\"background:#f9f9f9;\"><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">BBA</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">3 years</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">10+2 any stream 50% (45%)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">CUET / AUCET / Merit</td></tr>\r\n        <tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">BA / BCom / BSc</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">3 years</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">10+2 relevant stream 50% (45%)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">CUET / AUCET / Merit</td></tr>\r\n        <tr style=\"background:#f9f9f9;\"><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">BA LLB / BBA LLB (Integrated)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">5 years</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">10+2 any stream 50% (45%)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">CLAT / CUET / AUCET</td></tr>\r\n        <tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">LLB (3-year)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">3 years</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">Graduation 45% (40% reserved)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">CLAT / AUCET / Merit</td></tr>\r\n        <tr style=\"background:#f9f9f9;\"><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">BPT (Physiotherapy)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">4.5 years + internship</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">10+2 PCB 50% (45%)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">AUCET / Merit</td></tr>\r\n        <tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">B.Sc. Agriculture</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">4 years</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">10+2 PCB/PCM/Agriculture 50% (45%)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">JET (Rajasthan Agriculture) / AUCET</td></tr>\r\n        <tr style=\"background:#f9f9f9;\"><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">B.Sc. Nursing</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">4 years</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">10+2 PCB 50%; age ≤28 years on Dec 31</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">NEET / AUCET</td></tr>\r\n        <tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">B.Ed. / B.Ed. Special Education</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">2 years</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">Graduation with 50% (45%)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">AUCET / State B.Ed. Entrance</td></tr>\r\n      </tbody>\r\n    </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:0;\">\r\n    The most important note about <strong>Apex University Jaipur Courses</strong> at the UG level — specifically the <strong>Apex University UG Courses</strong> eligibility: the 50% and 45% thresholds (General vs reserved category) apply consistently across most programmes. The reserved category here refers to SC/ST/OBC/SBC candidates as per Rajasthan state reservation policy. BTech specifically requires PCM subjects at 10+2 level — BCA, BBA, and BA have broader stream flexibility.\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div id=\"pg-courses\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">Apex University PG Courses — Eligibility and Entry Routes</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <strong>Apex University PG Courses</strong> cover the full postgraduate range:\r\n  </p>\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li><strong>MBA:</strong> Graduation in any discipline with minimum 50% (45% reserved); accepted scores: CAT, MAT, CMAT, XAT, ATMA, CUET-PG, or AUCET; annual fee ₹90,000–₹1,80,000; 2 years</li>\r\n    <li><strong>MCA:</strong> Graduation with Mathematics (at 10+2 or graduation level); minimum 50% (45% reserved); CUET-PG or AUCET; total fee ₹2.2L; 2 years</li>\r\n    <li><strong>MTech:</strong> BTech/BE in relevant discipline with minimum 50% (45% reserved); GATE accepted and preferred; AUCET also accepted; 2 years</li>\r\n    <li><strong>LLM:</strong> LLB with minimum 50% (45% reserved); CLAT PG or AUCET; 1 year</li>\r\n    <li><strong>MSc / MA:</strong> Relevant BSc/BA with 50% (45% reserved); CUET-PG or AUCET or merit; 2 years</li>\r\n    <li><strong>MPT (Physiotherapy):</strong> BPT with 50% (45% reserved); AUCET; 2 years</li>\r\n    <li><strong>M.Ed.:</strong> B.Ed. or equivalent with 50%; State M.Ed. entrance or AUCET; 2 years</li>\r\n    <li><strong>PhD:</strong> PG degree with minimum 55% (50% for SC/ST/OBC with 5% relaxation); UGC-NET / GATE holders are exempt from the university entrance test; otherwise AUCET entrance + personal interview; 3–6 years full-time or part-time; available across Engineering, Sciences, Management, Law, Education, Allied Health, and Humanities</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:0;\">\r\n    The UGC-NET/GATE exemption for PhD is one of the more candidate-friendly features of <strong>Apex University Jaipur Courses</strong> at the doctoral level and is worth noting: holders of these national qualifications skip the university-level entrance test and proceed directly to the personal interview stage, which meaningfully shortens the admission timeline.\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"fees\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">Apex University Fees — Programme-Wise Breakdown</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <strong>Apex University Fees</strong> are among the lowest in Jaipur\'s private university segment, particularly for engineering and management:\r\n  </p>\r\n  <div style=\"overflow-x:auto;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;min-width:580px;font-size:14px;\">\r\n      <tbody>\r\n        <tr style=\"background:#3730a3;color:#fff;\"><th style=\"padding:10px;text-align:left;\">Programme</th><th style=\"padding:10px;text-align:left;\">Annual Fee</th><th style=\"padding:10px;text-align:left;\">Total (Approx.)</th></tr>\r\n        <tr style=\"background:#f9f9f9;\"><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">BTech</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹90,000–₹1,30,000</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹3.6L–₹6L (4 years)</td></tr>\r\n        <tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">MBA</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹90,000–₹1,80,000</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹1.8L–₹3.6L (2 years)</td></tr>\r\n        <tr style=\"background:#f9f9f9;\"><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">MCA</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹55,000/semester</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹2.2L (2 years)</td></tr>\r\n        <tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">BCA / BBA / BA / BCom / BSc</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹28,000–₹80,000</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹84,000–₹2.4L (3 years)</td></tr>\r\n        <tr style=\"background:#f9f9f9;\"><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">B.Sc. Agriculture</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹80,000</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹3.2L (4 years)</td></tr>\r\n        <tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">PhD (Academic Fee)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹60,000–₹80,000</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ddd;padding:10px;\">₹3.6L–₹5L (total academic)</td></tr>\r\n      </tbody>\r\n    </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li><strong>Application fee:</strong> ₹1,000 (online or demand draft)</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Registration fee:</strong> ₹10,000 — STRICTLY NON-REFUNDABLE once paid; confirm your programme and scholarship status before making this payment</li>\r\n    <li>All <strong>Apex University Fees</strong> above are for Indian/SAARC students for the 2026-27 academic session</li>\r\n    <li>CBSE students: percentage is calculated from main 5 subjects per CBSE policy, not from all subjects</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <div style=\"background:#fff8e6;border-left:4px solid #f59e0b;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;margin-top:16px;\">\r\n    <p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;font-size:14px;\"><strong>⚠ Fees Subject to Annual Revision:</strong> <strong>Apex University Fees</strong> above are based on the most recent published data. Always confirm exact 2026-27 fees for your specific programme directly with the Apex University admissions office before applying or planning your budget.</p>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"scholarships\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">Apex University Scholarships 2026 — All Eight Schemes</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <strong>Apex University Scholarships 2026</strong> are structured across eight distinct schemes. Before covering eligibility note: <strong>Apex University Eligibility</strong> rules apply uniformly. Three universal rules for <strong>Apex University Eligibility</strong> apply to all: scholarships are applied only on academic/course fees (never on application fee, registration fee, examination fee, uniform, or miscellaneous charges); UG scholarship slabs are based on Class 12 marks from the main five subjects; PG slabs are based on graduation aggregate marks.\r\n  </p>\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li><strong>Scheme 1 — AUCET-Based Scholarship:</strong> Awarded based on rank/score in the Apex University Common Entrance Test; higher AUCET scores unlock higher scholarship percentages up to 100% of course fee</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Scheme 2 — Merit-Based Scholarship (Academic Performance):</strong> Based on Class 12 aggregate percentage for UG admission; graduation aggregate for PG; typically tiered from 10% (60-70% marks range) to 100% (top performers)</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Scheme 3 — National Entrance-Based Scholarship:</strong> For candidates with valid scores in CUET, JEE Main, CAT, MAT, CMAT, XAT, CLAT, UCEED, or NIFT; scholarship percentage varies by score tier and programme</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Scheme 4 — Apex Shiksha Suraksha Yojana:</strong> For students from economically weaker sections; requires documentation of family income and financial need</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Scheme 5 — Sports Scholarship:</strong> For meritorious athletes who represented at state, national, or international level; sports achievement certificates required; renewal depends on continued sports performance post-admission</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Scheme 6 — Early Bird Scholarship:</strong> First-come-first-served; available for candidates applying in the early phases of the admission cycle; this window may have closed for 2026-27 — check directly with admissions office</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Scheme 7 — Loyalty / Sibling / Staff / CRPF Bonus:</strong> For siblings of current Apex students, children of Apex faculty/staff, and CRPF personnel families; specific percentages vary by category</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Scheme 8 — Armed Forces Educational Welfare Scheme:</strong> For wards of serving or retired Indian Armed Forces personnel; documentation of service required</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <div style=\"background:#f0fdf4;border-left:4px solid #15803d;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;margin-top:16px;\">\r\n    <p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;font-size:14px;\"><strong>✅ Key Rule:</strong> All <strong>Apex University Scholarships 2026</strong> must be applied for during the admission process — scholarships cannot be added in later years. The scholarship application deadline is October 31 each year for document submission. Only one scholarship scheme applies per student — if a candidate qualifies under multiple schemes, the highest percentage applies, not a combination.</p>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"application\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">Apex University Application Process — Step by Step</h2>\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    The complete <strong>Apex University Application Process</strong> for 2026-27:\r\n  </p>\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li><strong>Step 1 — Online Registration:</strong> Visit admissions.apexuniversity.co.in and click \"Apply Now\"; register with your name, email, mobile number, and Class 12/Graduation board details; or visit any Apex Admission Office or the Mansarovar campus for the offline <strong>Apex University Application Form</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Step 2 — Fill Application Form:</strong> Log in and complete the <strong>Apex University Application Form</strong> — the <strong>Apex University Application Form</strong> covers personal details, address, parent information, academic record, category, and programme choice; upload all required documents</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Step 3 — Document Upload:</strong> Photograph (passport size), signature, Class 10 marksheet, Class 12 marksheet (or Graduation marksheet for PG), category certificate (if applicable), Aadhaar/ID proof</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Step 4 — Pay Application Fee:</strong> ₹1,000 via online payment (net banking/card/UPI) or demand draft; fee is non-refundable</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Step 5 — AUCET / Score Submission:</strong> If applying through AUCET: book your exam slot and appear on the scheduled date; if applying through CUET, JEE Main, CAT, CLAT, NIFT, or other national tests: upload your valid scorecard</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Step 6 — Counselling and PI:</strong> Shortlisted candidates are called for counselling; MBA and PhD admissions include a Group Discussion and/or Personal Interview component</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Step 7 — Document Verification:</strong> Originals must be verified at the Apex Mansarovar Campus at the time of counselling and seat confirmation</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Step 8 — Pay Registration Fee and Confirm Seat:</strong> Pay the ₹10,000 registration fee (strictly non-refundable) to confirm your seat; apply for your scholarship at this stage — it cannot be added later</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n\r\n  <div style=\"background:#fff8e6;border-left:4px solid #f59e0b;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;margin-top:16px;\">\r\n    <p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;font-size:14px;\"><strong>⚠ Critical:</strong> The ₹10,000 registration fee in the <strong>Apex University Application Process</strong> is non-refundable under all circumstances. Do not pay this until you are certain of your programme choice, your eligibility, and have received confirmation of any scholarship being offered. This is the commitment point — everything before it is reversible.</p>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- ================= EXPLORE MORE GRID ================= -->\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:clamp(14px,3vw,20px);border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h3 style=\"margin-top:0;font-size:clamp(18px,3vw,22px);\">Explore More</h3>\r\n  <div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:12px;\">\r\n    <a href=\"https://www.collegenirnay.com/news/karnataka-2nd-puc-result-date-2026-live\" style=\"color:#fff;text-decoration:none;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5);border-radius:12px;min-height:64px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:12px;font-size:clamp(13px,2.8vw,14px);font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;transition:all .35s cubic-bezier(.17,.67,.83,.67);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35);\" onmouseover=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(-6px) scale(1.02)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 20px 40px rgba(55,48,163,.45)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#4338ca,#6366f1)\';\" onmouseout=\"this.style.transfor