\"color:#fff;text-decoration:none;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5);border-radius:12px;min-height:64px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:12px;font-size:clamp(13px,2.8vw,14px);font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;transition:all .35s cubic-bezier(.17,.67,.83,.67);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35);\"\r\n       onmouseover=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(-6px) scale(1.02)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 20px 40px rgba(55,48,163,.45)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#4338ca,#6366f1)\';\"\r\n       onmouseout=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(0) scale(1)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5)\';\">\r\n      Research Excellence\r\n    </a>\r\n\r\n    <a href=\"#\"\r\n       style=\"color:#fff;text-decoration:none;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5);border-radius:12px;min-height:64px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:12px;font-size:clamp(13px,2.8vw,14px);font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;transition:all .35s cubic-bezier(.17,.67,.83,.67);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35);\"\r\n       onmouseover=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(-6px) scale(1.02)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 20px 40px rgba(55,48,163,.45)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#4338ca,#6366f1)\';\"\r\n       onmouseout=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(0) scale(1)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5)\';\">\r\n      NEP 2020\r\n    </a>\r\n\r\n    <a href=\"#\"\r\n       style=\"color:#fff;text-decoration:none;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5);border-radius:12px;min-height:64px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:12px;font-size:clamp(13px,2.8vw,14px);font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;transition:all .35s cubic-bezier(.17,.67,.83,.67);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35);\"\r\n       onmouseover=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(-6px) scale(1.02)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 20px 40px rgba(55,48,163,.45)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#4338ca,#6366f1)\';\"\r\n       onmouseout=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(0) scale(1)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5)\';\">\r\n      Future of Higher Education\r\n    </a>\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>','/uploads/blogs/1785495476141-372213826.png',NULL,'Delhi University’s Top 200 Global Ranking Goal | QS Rankings & Future Plans','Explore Delhi University\'s plan to enter the world\'s top 200 universities by 2031. Learn about its QS Rankings growth, new postgraduate programmes, international collaborations, and academic transformation.',1,1,'2026-07-31 10:57:56','Blog ','Delhi University, QS World University Rankings, Higher Education India, Global University Rankings, School of Open Learning','Yash Bharadwaj','4',1,'published','2026-07-31 00:00:00'),(88,'Beyond Innovation: What IIT Madras Director V. Kamakoti\'s Role in India\'s Tech & Exam Reforms Means for Higher Education','iit-madras-director-v-kamakoti-tech-exam-reforms-higher-education','Explore how IIT Madras Director V. Kamakoti is shaping India\'s higher education landscape through technology-driven initiatives, examination reforms, AI integration, and academic innovation. Learn what these developments mean for students, universities, and the future of education in India.','<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\r\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n\r\n<title>Beyond Innovation: What IIT Madras Director V. Kamakoti\'s Role in India\'s Tech & Exam Reforms Means for Higher Education</title>\r\n\r\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"IIT Madras Director Prof. V. Kamakoti\'s role in Shakti microprocessor development and exam reforms highlights the growing link between technology, policy, and higher education in India.\">\r\n\r\n<style>\r\n  html {\r\n    scroll-behavior: smooth;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  summary::-webkit-details-marker {\r\n    display: none;\r\n  }\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin:0;\">\r\n    For years, India’s <strong>higher education</strong> conversation has focused on admissions, placements, and rankings. Today, the discussion is shifting toward something much bigger — how technology can strengthen education at a national level. The growing role of <strong>IIT Madras Director Prof. V. Kamakoti</strong> in major national initiatives, from India’s indigenous <strong>Shakti microprocessor</strong> programme to the government’s examination reform efforts, reflects this changing landscape. His work represents a broader trend where academic leaders are increasingly shaping public policy, technology development, and the future of higher education itself.\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">What We Cover</h2>\r\n\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;margin:0;\">\r\n    <li>\r\n      <a href=\"#innovation-leaders\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">\r\n        Universities Are Becoming Innovation Leaders\r\n      </a>\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <a href=\"#indigenous-technology\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">\r\n        The Rise of Indigenous Technology\r\n      </a>\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <a href=\"#exam-systems\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">\r\n        Technology Is Reshaping Examination Systems\r\n      </a>\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <a href=\"#student-impact\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">\r\n        Why This Matters for Students\r\n      </a>\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <a href=\"#national-asset\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">\r\n        Higher Education Is Becoming a Strategic National Asset\r\n      </a>\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <a href=\"#choose-university\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">\r\n        What Students Should Look for When Choosing a University\r\n      </a>\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <a href=\"#final-thoughts\" style=\"color:#3730a3;text-decoration:none;\">\r\n        Final Thoughts\r\n      </a>\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"innovation-leaders\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">\r\n    Universities Are Becoming Innovation Leaders\r\n  </h2>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    Modern universities are no longer confined to classrooms, laboratories, and traditional academic delivery. They are becoming active contributors to national development by solving real-world challenges through research, technology, innovation, and policy engagement.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    Institutions like <strong>IIT Madras</strong> demonstrate how higher education can contribute to areas that go far beyond regular teaching and degree programmes.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Indigenous technology development:</strong> Universities can help build technologies that strengthen national capability.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Semiconductor and chip innovation:</strong> Academic research can support India’s long-term goals in advanced electronics.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Artificial Intelligence research:</strong> Institutions can explore AI applications across education, industry, governance, and society.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Digital infrastructure:</strong> Universities can support systems that improve access, transparency, and efficiency.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>National education reforms:</strong> Academic experts can help design better systems for learning, assessment, and governance.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Cybersecurity and technology governance:</strong> Higher education institutions can contribute to safer and more accountable digital systems.\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:0;\">\r\n    The growing involvement of academic institutions in these areas highlights the expanding role universities play beyond teaching and research. They are becoming centres of innovation, policy contribution, and national problem-solving.\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <p>\r\n    <strong>Related Article:</strong>\r\n\r\n    <a href=\"#\" style=\"display:inline-block;background:#3730a3;color:#fff;padding:10px 20px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin-top:12px;\">\r\n      Explore More Higher Education Innovation Insights\r\n    </a>\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"indigenous-technology\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">\r\n    The Rise of Indigenous Technology\r\n  </h2>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    One of Prof. V. Kamakoti’s most recognised contributions has been his leadership in India’s <strong>Shakti microprocessor</strong> initiative. This effort is aimed at strengthening India’s technological self-reliance through indigenous processor design.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    The project aligns with the country’s broader focus on reducing dependence on imported technologies while encouraging domestic innovation, research, and advanced engineering capability.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    For students, this signals an important shift. Future careers are increasingly emerging in areas such as:\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Semiconductor design:</strong> Students can explore careers connected with chip architecture, processor design, and hardware systems.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Embedded systems:</strong> This field connects software, hardware, electronics, and real-world device applications.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>AI hardware:</strong> As AI grows, specialised hardware for faster and more efficient computing will become increasingly important.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Cybersecurity:</strong> Secure hardware and digital systems will be essential for national, industrial, and institutional safety.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Electronics manufacturing:</strong> India’s push for domestic technology development can create new opportunities in electronics production and design.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>High-performance computing:</strong> Advanced computing systems will support research, data processing, simulations, and emerging technologies.\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:0;\">\r\n    Universities that integrate these domains into their curriculum will be better positioned to prepare graduates for tomorrow’s workforce. Indigenous technology development is not only a national goal; it is also an academic and career opportunity for students.\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"exam-systems\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">\r\n    Technology Is Reshaping Examination Systems\r\n  </h2>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    India’s examination ecosystem has expanded significantly over the past few decades. National entrance tests now serve millions of students every year, making transparency, security, scalability, and accountability more important than ever.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    Prof. Kamakoti’s participation in the government’s examination reform task force reflects a growing emphasis on using technology to build a more secure, transparent, and reliable assessment system.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    Examination reform can involve several important areas:\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Secure digital systems:</strong> Technology can help strengthen examination security and reduce vulnerabilities.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Transparent processes:</strong> Better systems can improve trust among students, parents, institutions, and policymakers.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Scalable infrastructure:</strong> National-level examinations require systems that can handle large numbers of students efficiently.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Improved logistics:</strong> Technology can support better planning, monitoring, centre allocation, and process management.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Stronger governance:</strong> Expert oversight can help ensure that examination systems remain accountable and fair.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Data-driven monitoring:</strong> Digital systems can help identify patterns, risks, delays, and areas for improvement.\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:0;\">\r\n    Rather than viewing technology as a replacement for human expertise, the approach focuses on combining digital systems with expert oversight to improve trust, efficiency, and fairness in large-scale assessments.\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"student-impact\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">\r\n    Why This Matters for Students\r\n  </h2>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    Education is becoming increasingly technology-driven, not only inside classrooms but also across admissions, examinations, academic administration, research, and career development.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    Students should expect future universities to offer learning environments that are more digital, research-focused, secure, and industry-connected.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>AI-enabled learning environments:</strong> Students may experience personalised learning, intelligent academic support, and better access to digital resources.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Digital assessment systems:</strong> Exams and evaluations may become more technology-enabled and data-supported.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Secure examination processes:</strong> Stronger systems can help protect the credibility of admissions and assessments.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Industry-integrated curriculum:</strong> Academic programmes can become more aligned with emerging sectors and workforce needs.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Research-driven learning:</strong> Students can engage more deeply with innovation, experimentation, and problem-solving.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Innovation-focused academic ecosystems:</strong> Universities can support startups, product development, technology projects, and interdisciplinary learning.\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:0;\">\r\n    These developments are preparing learners for workplaces where technology, data, research, and digital decision-making will play a central role in everyday professional life.\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"national-asset\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">\r\n    Higher Education Is Becoming a Strategic National Asset\r\n  </h2>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    India’s universities are no longer simply producing graduates. They are contributing to national priorities such as technological innovation, digital transformation, workforce development, research, entrepreneurship, and public policy.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    As academic leaders increasingly participate in policy, research, and technology missions, the relationship between higher education and national development continues to strengthen.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li>\r\n      Universities can support India’s technological self-reliance through research and innovation.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      Academic experts can help design better systems for education, examinations, and digital governance.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      Research institutions can contribute to AI, semiconductor technology, cybersecurity, and advanced computing.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      Students can gain access to emerging fields through future-ready academic programmes.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      Innovation ecosystems can support entrepreneurship, startups, and product development.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      Higher education can help build a skilled workforce for India’s next phase of growth.\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:0;\">\r\n    This evolution creates greater opportunities for students to engage in research, innovation, entrepreneurship, and emerging technology sectors while still pursuing their academic goals.\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"choose-university\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">\r\n    What Students Should Look for When Choosing a University\r\n  </h2>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    As higher education evolves, students should evaluate institutions based on more than reputation, rankings, location, or placement claims. The best universities are those that prepare learners for long-term success in a technology-driven world.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    Students should consider whether a university:\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Encourages research and innovation:</strong> Does the institution support student projects, labs, publications, and academic inquiry?\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Integrates emerging technologies:</strong> Are AI, data, cybersecurity, electronics, robotics, and digital tools part of the learning experience?\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Collaborates with industry and government:</strong> Does the university connect students with real-world challenges, public missions, and professional opportunities?\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Offers practical learning opportunities:</strong> Are internships, live projects, case studies, hackathons, and applied assignments available?\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Supports entrepreneurship and innovation:</strong> Are incubation centres, startup support, mentoring, and innovation labs accessible to students?\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Builds future-ready digital skills:</strong> Does the curriculum prepare students for technology-driven workplaces and continuous learning?\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Provides strong academic mentorship:</strong> Are students guided by faculty and experts who are active in research, innovation, or policy?\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      <strong>Focuses on long-term employability:</strong> Does the university prepare students for future industries, not only immediate job opportunities?\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:0;\">\r\n    These factors often provide a clearer picture of how effectively an institution prepares students for future careers, emerging industries, and meaningful professional growth.\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"final-thoughts\" style=\"scroll-margin-top:30vh;border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:20px;border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h2 style=\"margin-top:0;\">\r\n    Final Thoughts\r\n  </h2>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    The growing role of academic leaders like <strong>Prof. V. Kamakoti</strong> illustrates how higher education is expanding beyond classrooms and campuses. Universities are becoming centres of innovation, technology development, examination reform, and national problem-solving.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    As India continues investing in digital infrastructure, semiconductor technology, AI, and examination reforms, students stand to benefit from an education system that is increasingly connected to real-world challenges.\r\n  </p>\r\n\r\n  <ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:14px;\">\r\n    <li>\r\n      Universities are becoming active contributors to national technology missions.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      Indigenous innovation is creating new career opportunities for students.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      Examination reforms highlight the importance of secure and transparent education systems.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      Students should look for institutions that combine academics with research, technology, and practical exposure.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      Higher education is becoming a strategic part of India’s future growth.\r\n    </li>\r\n\r\n    <li>\r\n      The next phase of education will depend on innovation, adaptability, and real-world problem-solving.\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n\r\n  <p style=\"line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:0;\">\r\n    The future of higher education will not be defined solely by the degrees universities award. It will be defined by how effectively they prepare students to innovate, adapt, and contribute to India’s next era of technological growth.\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<!-- ================= EXPLORE MORE GRID ================= -->\r\n\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #e6e6e6;padding:clamp(14px,3vw,20px);border-radius:1rem;margin-bottom:40px;\">\r\n  <h3 style=\"margin-top:0;font-size:clamp(18px,3vw,22px);\">\r\n    Explore More\r\n  </h3>\r\n\r\n  <div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:12px;\">\r\n\r\n    <a href=\"#\"\r\n       style=\"color:#fff;text-decoration:none;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5);border-radius:12px;min-height:64px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:12px;font-size:clamp(13px,2.8vw,14px);font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;transition:all .35s cubic-bezier(.17,.67,.83,.67);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35);\"\r\n       onmouseover=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(-6px) scale(1.02)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 20px 40px rgba(55,48,163,.45)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#4338ca,#6366f1)\';\"\r\n       onmouseout=\"this.style.transform=\'translateY(0) scale(1)\';this.style.boxShadow=\'0 6px 18px rgba(55,48,163,.35)\';this.style.background=\'linear-gradient(135deg,#3730a3,#4f46e5)\';\">\r\n      IIT Madras\r\n    </a>\r\n\r\n    <a href